---
description: Name functions so the return type is obvious at the call site
alwaysApply: true
---

# Naming and return type

Name a function after what it returns (or clearly does), so callers need not open the signature.

```ts
// BAD — sounds like a role, returns an Account
viewerFromHeader(header, db, secret);

// GOOD
accountFromHeader(header, db, secret);
```

Context keys may still say `viewer` when that is the role in the request. The helper that builds the value should still name the value (`account`, `userId`, `token`, …).

Prefer concrete result types over vague bags at boundaries.
